    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Architectural History",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The church, designed with a continuous nave and chancel in the ‘perpendicular’ (late Gothic) style by G. F. Bodley, was built in 1894-95.",
                "The construction is of stone, but the Tower planned for the south-west corner was never built. The interior is tall with slim Perpendicular columns and elegant detailing in stone. There is no clerestory.",
                "G F Bodley (1827-1907) was a leading ecclesiastical architect of the period in the area. The stonework detail on the nave arcades is particularly interesting.\nAn interesting feature is the ceiling which has verses from the bible inscribed around the ceiling area.\nSome of the stained glass was designed by Charles Kempe, and the pipe organ was built by Norman and Beard"
            ]
        }
    ],
